message.content:
{"translation": "A freshly tuned verse, a cup of wine,
Last year's old weather, old pavilions still.
The sun sets west—when will it rise again?

Helplessly the blossoms fall and fade;
As if once seen, the swallows come again.
Alone I pace the scented paths of the small garden."}

{"translation": "# Spring View

The kingdom falls—the hills and rivers stand.
Spring fills the city; grass and trees run wild.
Touched by the times, the flowers seem to weep;
At parting's grief, the birds my heart alarm.

Beacon fires have burned for three long months;
A letter from my home is worth ten thousand gold.
I scratch my thinning white-haired head—
It scarcely holds a hairpin anymore."}

{"translation": "# Wuling Spring: Late Spring

The wind has stilled, fragrant dust where petals fell;
The sun hangs low, too weary to dress my hair.
All things remain, but you are gone forever —
I wish to speak, yet tears come first instead.

I hear they say spring still graces Shuangxi;
I too would drift along in a light boat.
But I fear the little boats of Shuangxi
Cannot bear so much sorrow afloat."}

# Spring View

The state lies broken; mountains, rivers stay;
Spring fills the city — grasses run wild and deep.
Time stirs the flowers, splashing tears;
Parting makes the birds' cries startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned three months unceasing;
A letter home outweighs ten thousand gold.
My white hair scratches ever thinner —
So thin it can no longer hold a pin in place.

