Amid the ruins, mountains and rivers remain;
In spring, the city is overgrown with grass and trees.
Grieved by the times, flowers weep with tears;
Hating parting, birds' cries alarm the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three long months;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand gold.
White hair grows thinner as I scratch my head;
So thin, it barely holds a hairpin.

