message.content:
{"translation":"Spring Gazing

The capital lies in ruins, yet mountains and rivers remain;
In spring, the city is deep with grass and trees.
Grieving the times, the flowers weep; hating parting, the birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires burn for three long months; a home letter is worth ten thousand gold.
My white hair, scratched, grows ever shorter, so frail I cannot bear a hairpin."}

