message.content:
The nation's wrecked, mountains and rivers still stand;  
The city in spring, grass and trees are deep.  
Saddened by the times, flowers weep;  
Hating parting, birds alarm the heart.  
Beacon fires burn through three long months;  
A home letter is worth ten thousand gold.  
White hair, I scratch, grows thinner and thinner;  
Barely able to hold a hairpin.

