Wind swift, sky high, ape's mournful cry;  
Islet clear, sand white, birds wheel back.  
Boundless falling leaves rustle down,  
Endless Yangtze surges on.  
Ten thousand miles of autumn sorrow, wanderer ever;  
Long years of illness, alone on the terrace.  
Hardships and bitter hate, frost on temples;  
Down and out, I've just stopped the turbid wine.

