Broken is the nation, yet mountains and rivers remain;  
In the city, spring fills with deep grass and trees.  
Grieved by the times, flowers splash tears;  
Hating parting, birds alarm the heart.  
Beacon fires burn for three months straight;  
A letter from home is worth ten thousand in gold.  
My white hair grows thinner and thinner,  
I can barely hold a hairpin.

