On Xunyang's riverbank, a night of farewell to guests,  
Maple leaves and reeds in autumn's shiver.  
The host dismounts, the guest on boat;  
Wine raised, no strings to play.  
Drunk, joy turns to sorrow as we part;  
The river, moon reflected, dims.  
Suddenly, a pipa's sound on water;  
Host forgets return, guest stays put.  
Seeking the sound, softly asked who played;  
Pipa stops, words hesitate.  
Move the boat near, invite to meet;  
Add wine, light lamps, renew the feast.  
Thousand calls, finally she appears;  
Still half-hiding, pipa held.  
Tune the axis, pluck a few strings;  
Before the tune, emotion flows.  
Each string, a suppressed note;  
Each sound, a thought; like sorrowing of life unfulfilled.  
Bowed head, fingers move;  
All hidden thoughts are spoken.  
Gently sweep, gently pluck, then slide and lift;  
First the Rainbow Skirt, then Liu Yao.  
Thick strings roar like sudden rain;  
Thin strings whisper like private talk.  
Roar and whisper mix;  
Pearls drop on jade plate.  
Like oriole's song through flowers, smooth;  
Like choked spring under ice, hard.  
Cold spring, strings stiff, stop;  
Silence hangs.  
Another deep sorrow grows;  
Silence speaks louder than sound.  
Silver bottle shatters, water gushes;  
Iron cavalry charges, swords clash.  
End of tune, pick drawn across heart;  
Four strings, one sound, like tearing silk.  
East and west ships silent;  
Only autumn moon white on river's heart.  
Musing, place pick in strings;  
Adjust robes, face serious.  
She says: "Born in capital, home beneath Xia Ma Ling."  
Thirteen learned pipa well;  
Name first in teaching hall.  
After tune, Shancai bowed;  
Makeup, every time Qiu Niang envied.  
Wuling youths vied for gifts;  
One tune, red silk countless.  
Hairpin silver comb broke to beat;  
Blood-red silk skirt stained with wine.  
Happy laughter year by year;  
Autumn moon, spring breeze, wasted.  
Brother left to war, aunt died;  
Days pass, face grows old.  
Door cold, few riders;  
Old, married merchant's wife.  
Merchant values profit, light on parting;  
Last month, Fú Liáng bought tea.  
Go and return, guard empty boat;  
Moon bright, river cold.  
Deep night, dream of youth;  
Dream weeps, makeup tears red.  
I heard pipa, sighed;  
Heard this, sighed again.  
Both lost souls on earth;  
Meet, no need to know before!  
I left capital last year;  
Exiled, sick in Xunyang.  
Xunyang remote, no music;  
Whole year, no strings or bamboo sounds.  
Near Pén River, land low and wet;  
Yellow reeds, bitter bamboo round my home.  
What do I hear day and night?  
Cuckoo bleeds, monkeys wail.  
Spring river, flower day, autumn moon night;  
Often drink alone.  
No mountain songs, village flutes?  
Guttural, harsh, hard to bear.  
Tonight, hearing your pipa,  
Like heavenly music, ears bright.  
Do not refuse, sit again, play one more;  
For you, I write this "Pipa Song".  
Moved by your words, long stood;  
Then sat, strings quickened.  
Sorrowful, not like before;  
All hear again, weep.  
Who wept most in the hall?  
Jiangzhou's governor, his green robe wet.

