Wind swift, sky high, apes wail mournfully;
Islet clear, sand white, birds wheel back.
Endless falling leaves rustle down;
Inexhaustible Yangtze River rolls on.
Sorrowful autumn for ten thousand miles, I am a guest;
A hundred years of illness, alone on the platform.
Hardship and bitter hatred, thick frost on temples;
Downtrodden, newly stopped the muddy wine cup.

