{"translation":"A new verse set to music, a cup of wine,  
The same weather as last year, the old pavilion.  
Westward sinks the sun—when will it return?  
Helplessly, flowers fall;  
Like a long-lost friend, swallows come back again.  
Alone, I pace the fragrant path in the garden."}

